🔧 MAC 5000 Assembly Guide (Per Schematic Section)


---

A1 – Power Distribution & Protection

Objective: Safely route all high-current lines (AC & DC) and install protective components before signal wiring.

Components:

Alternator/Inverter unit

ANL 50 A main fuse + holder

DC bus bar (covered, copper)

AC breaker bank (2 × 15 A 120 V, 1 × 20 A 240 V)

MOV surge absorbers

Ground/neutral bars

AC receptacles (NEMA 5-15R × 2, 6-20R × 1)


Assembly Steps:

1. Mount the Breaker Bank

Left interior wall of the enclosure, vertical orientation.

Torque terminals to 2.3 N·m.



2. Install the ANL Fuse Holder within 150 mm of the 12 V source.


3. Attach the DC Bus Bar on insulating standoffs; cover with clear Lexan guard.


4. Connect 12 V Source → ANL → DC Bus using 10 AWG red wire; crimp ring lugs (AMP yellow insulated).


5. Install MOVs: one across L–N, one L–PE, one N–PE at AC bus input.


6. Mount Ground & Neutral Bars on aluminum chassis; scrape paint under bonding points.


7. Wire Breakers to Outlets following color codes (black L1, red L2, white N, green PE).


8. Label each breaker and outlet with engraved tags (“120 V R1”, “240 V R”).




---

A2 – Control Panel & Latching Relay

Objective: Assemble the front-panel controls and safety interlock loop.

Components:

Front panel (from DXF)

ON/OFF toggle switch

START momentary pushbutton

SERVO brake potentiometer (knob)

E-STOP mushroom switch (latching)

12 V RESET button

LCD display module

Latching relay (40 A contacts, 12 V coil)


Assembly Steps:

1. Fabricate panel from 3–4 mm Al using DXF template; deburr holes.


2. Install switches and buttons; secure with locking nuts (hand-tight + ¼ turn).


3. Mount LCD using M3 × 8 mm screws and nylon spacers.


4. Wire E-STOP Loop:

E-STOP → MCU_OK → LATCH coil − (series).

Coil + from DC bus via fuse.



5. Wire ON/OFF toggle to MCU enable (5 V logic line).


6. Connect START momentary to MCU start input (via debounce RC network).


7. Run shielded cable from brake knob pot to MCU ADC input.


8. Verify switch orientation before mounting panel onto enclosure (face plate right-side up).


9. Secure latching relay near bus bars on DIN rail; connect contact outputs to main drive/excitation feed.




---

A3 – Servo Brake Drive

Objective: Install servo actuator and linkage to the magnetic brake lever.

Components:

Metal-gear servo (25–35 kg·cm torque)

Servo bracket & mount hardware

Lever arm (G10 5 mm)

Linear guide rail carriage for flux-shunt blade

Return spring and silicone bump stops


Assembly Steps:

1. Attach servo to bracket using M4 × 12 mm screws and thread-locker (blue).


2. Mount bracket to chassis plate (4 mm Al); torque 2 N·m.


3. Install 25T horn and lever arm; verify center neutral position at 90°.


4. Connect lever to shunt blade carriage with M3 rod end and clevis pin.


5. Set spring so that at power loss the lever returns to brake position.


6. Route servo wiring (16 AWG twisted) through braided sleeving to servo driver.


7. Test actuation: MCU PWM 0–100 % → lever travel 8–12 mm range.


8. Install Mu-metal shield if within 100 mm of core magnetic field.




---

A4 – Sensor Pod & Telemetry

Objective: Deploy sensors for feedback and monitoring.

Components:

Hall-effect RPM sensor + magnet flag

NTC temp sensors (core & bearing)

AC voltage/frequency isolation board

Wiring harness (22 AWG shielded pairs)


Assembly Steps:

1. Mount Hall sensor 3–5 mm from flywheel target; align radially.


2. Epoxy magnet flag onto non-ferrous flywheel surface (2-part epoxy spray).


3. Place temp sensors with Kapton tape + thermal compound on bearing housing and core plate.


4. Install isolation board on standoffs in sensor bay; connect AC tap leads through fused resistor divider.


5. Run shielded cables to MCU I/O header; ground shields at MCU end only.


6. Confirm readings: RPM pulse train clean (< 50 mVpp noise), temp sensors < 1 °C error vs reference.




---

A5 – Output Panel & Receptacles

Objective: Wire and mount the load-side outputs with proper safety clearances.

Components:

2 × NEMA 5-15R receptacles (120 V)

1 × NEMA 6-20R (240 V)

Grounding bus bar

Labels and faceplate hardware


Assembly Steps:

1. Cut and deburr faceplate openings; mount receptacles flush with panel.


2. Wire 120 V outlets: 14 AWG black (L), white (N), green (PE).


3. Wire 240 V outlet: 12 AWG black (L1), red (L2), green (PE).


4. Install individual breakers in-line with each hot lead.


5. Bond grounds to star ground stud (M6 serrated washer stack).


6. Apply labels with voltage rating and breaker current.


7. Perform continuity and polarity test before energizing.




---

Final System Checks

Torque Audit: verify all screw and lug torques per spec.

Continuity: ring-out each harness vs schematic netlist.

Insulation Test: 500 V megger AC circuits (disconnect electronics).

Ground bond: < 0.1 Ω from each panel to star ground.

Functional: Power ON → Start → Brake Test → E-Stop → Reset.
